Description: Run an application on the GPU the system's graphics settings choose
 An application whose desktop entry does not say where it runs asks the
 Graphics page's resolver, sparky-stereo-gpu-env --app with its menu id (or
 its desktop file when it is outside the menu), and starts with the
 variables it answers: DRI_PRIME, the Vulkan driver selection, NVIDIA's
 render offload. The entry's own PrefersNonDefaultGPU (and the older
 X-KDE-RunOnDiscreteGpu) keeps KIO's own handling, and a GPU already chosen
 in the launch environment (DRI_PRIME, MESA_VK_DEVICE_SELECT,
 VK_LOADER_DRIVERS_SELECT, __NV_PRIME_RENDER_OFFLOAD) wins. When the command
 is missing, fails or does not answer within two seconds, the application
 starts as before. Tests with a stand-in resolver are added to
 applicationlauncherjobtest.
Author: Daniel Ramos (Capitain Jack) <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Forwarded: not-needed, edition-only (the resolver is Sparky Stereo OS's Graphics page)
Last-Update: 2026-10-24

